// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 06-arithmetic
// facility: rule.arith.literal [Literal-Out-Of-Range] (conf.negated-literal-parenthesized)
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.literal-out-of-range (static)
//
// `[Literal-Negated]` applies only where the minus is applied directly
// to the literal. Inside parentheses, 2147483648 is an ordinary i32
// literal, and it is out of range before any negation.

fn main()
{
    -(2147483648);
}
